+</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Garden City is not a town. It has no mayor, no town council and no town police. The Census Bureau counts it as a "census designated place", its name for a community with no government of its own, and counted 10,235 people there in 2020.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Horry and Georgetown county line crosses the beach about a third of a mile south of the Garden City Pier. The pier and the Census place are in Horry County. About 3.2 of Waccamaw Drive's 5 miles run south of the line, in Georgetown County, to Garden City Point at the inlet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county decides your property tax, your rental license and the beach rules. Most addresses use Murrells Inlet and ZIP code 29576; a band at the north edge uses Surfside Beach, 29575. None of it is part of the City of Myrtle Beach.</p><figure class="c3-gc-fig"><div class="c3-gc-frame"><svg class="c3-gc-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 2141" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-gc-map-t"><title id="c3-gc-map-t">Aerial map of Garden City, South Carolina: the beach road, Waccamaw Drive, runs along the ocean with salt marsh behind it. The Horry and Georgetown county line crosses the beach a little south of the pier, and most of the beach road lies south of it, in Georgetown County, down to Garden City Point at the inlet. Business 17 runs inland. Numbers 1 to 5 mark the five parts described below.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-aerial-1000.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="2141" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M1285 -170.6L1301.4 -188.9M1402.7 -307L1466.2 -381M1481.5 -398.9L1482.3 -399.9M1269.2 -152.4L1262.2 -144M1262.2 -144L12