lass="lb it" x="450.8" y="1256.3" text-anchor="middle">Salt marsh</text><text class="lb" x="200.1" y="2041.1" text-anchor="start">Garden City Point</text><text class="lb" x="1352.5" y="97.1" text-anchor="end">Surfside Beach</text><g transform="translate(1053.6 622.5)"><circle r="40" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="7"/><text class="pn" y="20" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g><g transform="translate(830.5 679.6)"><circle r="40" fill="#2f6f8f" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="7"/><text class="pn" y="20" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g><g transform="translate(676.3 599.7)"><circle r="40" fill="#5f8a4e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="7"/><text class="pn" y="20" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g><g transform="translate(616.9 171.3)"><circle r="40" fill="#8a5a9e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="7"/><text class="pn" y="20" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g><g transform="translate(367.8 1598.8)"><circle r="40" fill="#b3261e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="7"/><text class="pn" y="20" text-anchor="middle">5</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>The dashed line is the county line. About 3.2 of Waccamaw Drive's 5 miles are south of it, in Georgetown County. Aerial: USGS The National Map, orthoimagery (USDA NAIP), public domain. Lines: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line, Horry County GIS and OpenStreetMap. Labels: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption><ol class="c3-gc-key" aria-label="The five parts of Garden City"><li><span class="c3-gc-num p1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span><a href="#ocean-side">The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive</a>: the beach and the pier</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span><a href="#on-the-marsh">On the marsh</a>: salt marsh out back, the highest prices on the creek side</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span><a href="#older-streets">Between the marsh and Business 17</a>: the most kinds of homes</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span><a href="#west-of-17">West of Business 17</a>: no high-risk flood zone</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p5" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span><a href="#georgetown-end">The Georgetown end</a>: the quietest stretch of beach road</span></li></ol></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="parts"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Five parts">Which part of Garden City fits you?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Garden City has five parts, and they differ more than most towns do. The numbers match the map above. Each price is what homes there sold for in the past year, from county deeds.</p><h3 id="ocean-side" data-toc="The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive: the beach and the pier</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes between Waccamaw Drive and the ocean have the beach at the back door. About 1,400 homes stand here on the Horry side, and about 1,240 of them are condo units. Only 48 are houses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Garden City Pier is the center of this side. It runs 668 feet into the ocean, and bands play at both ends of it every night, weather permitting. In summer, fishing on the pier runs around the clock. The pier pass covers it, so no state fishing license is needed there.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-pier-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-pier-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-pier-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Garden City Beach, labelled: the Garden City Pier running into the Atlantic Ocean, buildings and beach houses along Waccamaw Drive, and Atlantic Avenue crossing the salt marsh" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The ocean side by the pier from above: buildings and beach houses between Waccamaw Drive and the beach, and the salt marsh behind.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of these homes are second homes or rentals. The county mails the tax bill for 57 percent of them to another state, North Carolina, New York, Pennsylvania and Ohio most often. In the past year, 55 of 86 condos sold here went to buyers whose tax bill goes out of state.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The trade-off is water: almost every home on this side is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. An ocean-side condo sold for about $320,000 at the middle, and half sold for between about $265,000 and $440,000.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City's%20ocean%20side">Get the condos for sale on Garden City's ocean side<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="on-the-marsh" data-toc="On the marsh" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>On the marsh: salt marsh out back</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Behind the beach strip lies salt marsh, cut by tidal creeks that reach the inlet at Garden City Point. About 260 houses between Waccamaw Drive and Business 17 sit on the marsh or a tidal creek, along both edges of it. At our last count, 7 homes for sale in the Garden City area listed a private dock.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-marsh-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-marsh-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-marsh-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the salt marsh at Garden City at high tide, with long private docks running out from houses on the mainland at left and on the beach strip at lower right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The salt marsh behind the beach strip, with docks from the houses on both edges.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These are the most costly houses on this side of Waccamaw Drive. The 13 marsh-front houses that sold in the past year went for about $1.24 million at the middle, about twice the other houses there. Few come up for sale, which is the trade-off.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City">Get the marsh-front homes for sale in Garden City<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="older-streets" data-toc="Between the marsh and Business 17" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>Between the marsh and Business 17: the most kinds of homes</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of the marsh, streets of houses, condos and manufactured homes run back to Business 17. About 3,000 homes stand here, about half of them houses, and about half of the houses are taxed as the owner's main home. This part also takes in the streets north of where Waccamaw Drive ends, up to the Surfside Beach town line.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-streets-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-streets-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-streets-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of streets of houses under trees in Garden City, with a pond at the top and the salt marsh at the lower right, labelled" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Streets between the marsh and Business 17 from above: houses and yards, a pond, and the salt marsh at the lower right.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lowest asking prices east of Business 17 are on manufactured homes, from about $80,000. Their middle ask here is about $257,000, and the lot rent, where there is one, is not in the price. We find out for each home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About half the homes here are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. A house sold for about $575,000 at the middle in the past year, and a condo for about $225,000.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City%20east%20of%20Business%2017">Get the homes for sale in Garden City east of Business 17<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-of-17" data-toc="West of Business 17" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>West of Business 17: no high-risk flood zone</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of Business 17 are Garden City's subdivisions, with about 3,100 homes. None of them is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, the only part of Garden City where that is true. About 3 in 4 houses here are taxed as the owner's main home, the most of any part. Most of the addresses that say Surfside Beach, 29575, are here, at the north edge.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-west-of-17-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-west-of-17-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-west-of-17-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of subdivisions west of Business 17 in Garden City: houses on curving streets around ponds, a swimming pool and sports courts, with woods at the upper right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Subdivisions west of Business 17 from above: houses on curving streets, ponds, a pool and courts, and woods.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach is on the other side of Business 17. A house here sold for about $340,000 at the middle in the past year and a condo for about $173,000, the lowest prices in Garden City. Manufactured homes for sale here ask about $140,000 at the middle.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City%20west%20of%20Business%2017">Get the homes for sale in Garden City west of Business 17<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="georgetown-end" data-toc="The Georgetown end" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p5" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span>The Georgetown end: the quietest stretch of beach road</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South of the county line, Waccamaw Drive runs about 3.2 more miles to Garden City Point, where the marsh meets the inlet. On Census Day 2020, only about 1 in 6 homes along this stretch had someone living in it.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-point-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-point-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-point-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the south end of Garden City Beach, labelled: houses on curving canals with private docks between the inlet water at left and Waccamaw Drive and the Atlantic Ocean at right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Georgetown end near Garden City Point from above: houses on canals with private docks, Waccamaw Drive and the beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Georgetown County's rules apply here, not Horry's. It requires no business license for a rental, and its lodging tax is lower. Horry County lends beach wheelchairs free, but not on this end.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It has the highest asking prices in Garden City. At our last count, 24 listings were for sale here at a middle ask of about $1.45 million, and its 8 ocean-side houses asked about $2.9 million.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City's%20Georgetown%20end">Get the homes for sale at Garden City's Georgetown end<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes in Garden City cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo on the ocean side sold for about $320,000 at the middle in the past year. Houses ran from about $340,000 west of Business 17 to about $1.24 million on the marsh.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a home in Garden City sold for in the past year, at the middle"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a home in Garden City sold for in the past year, at the middle</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part and kind of home, how many sold</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">On the marsh, houses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">13 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,240,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Between the marsh and Business 17, houses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">57 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.465" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$575,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of Business 17, houses</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">57 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.275" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$340,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ocean side, condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">89 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.259" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$320,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Between the marsh and Business 17, condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">37 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.182" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$225,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of Business 17, condos</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">121 sold</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.139" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$173,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Horry County deeds; the Georgetown end's sales are not in this count. Only three ocean-side houses sold, for $1.3 million to $2.35 million.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At our last count, 195 listings were for sale in Garden City: 73 condos, 49 houses and 67 manufactured homes, plus a few lots and small apartment buildings. Ocean-side condos on the Horry side asked about $377,000 at the middle, about $406 a square foot.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Asking prices run above sale prices. We pull the recent sales in the same building or on the same street before you make an offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="airbnb"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you Airbnb in Garden City, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There is no town rule against it, because there is no town. Horry County's own list of what an owner must file to rent short term, outside any city, names no rental permit. The building's own rules can still say no. The county's list names four filings:</p><ol style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">A county business license.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">A state sales tax number, from the South Carolina Department of Revenue.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">A county hospitality and accommodations account, which the county opens for you.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">A yearly business personal property return, form PT-100, by April 30.</li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Guests pay about 12 percent in lodging taxes on the Horry side: 9 percent collected by the state and the county's 3 percent hospitality fee. On the Georgetown end, guests pay about 11 percent: 8 percent to the state and Georgetown County's 3 percent. A stay of 90 days or more is not taxed as lodging, and Georgetown County's 3 percent stops at 30 days. Our <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">accommodations tax guide</a> shows how to file.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo association or an HOA (homeowners association) can forbid or limit rentals in its own papers. We read the master deed and the rules for the exact building before you offer. Our page on <a href="/hoa/rental-restrictions/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA rental restrictions</a> explains how those rules work.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a Garden City Airbnb earns</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI counted 374 active Airbnb listings in Garden City Beach over the past 12 months, and found a permit number on none of them.</p><ul class="c3-gc-stats" aria-label="Airbnb numbers for Garden City Beach, past 12 months"><li><b>$41,200</b><span>average listing's revenue in a year</span></li><li><b>40%</b><span>of nights booked</span></li><li><b>$371</b><span>average nightly rate</span></li><li><b>$3,470</b><span>a typical listing's month</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of the money comes in summer. A listing earns about 5 times as much in an average July as in January, and about 65 percent of nights were booked last July against about 25 percent in January.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a Garden City Beach Airbnb earns in an average month"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a Garden City Beach Airbnb earns in an average month</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Month</span><span role="columnheader">Revenue</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">January</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.205" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,090</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">February</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.276" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,820</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">March</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.359" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3,660</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">April</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.43" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$4,390</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">May</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.555" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$5,660</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">June</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.852" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$8,690</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">July</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$10,200</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">August</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.641" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$6,540</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">September</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.404" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$4,120</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">October</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.342" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3,490</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">November</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.269" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,740</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">December</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.262" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,670</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>AirROI's average revenue per active listing, by month, over two years. Before cleaning, platform fees, management and taxes.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: the middle ocean-side condo, rented by the night</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take a condo on the ocean side at the middle price, about $320,000, that earns what a typical Garden City Beach listing earns. No loan is in this example.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>One year of nightly renting, the middle ocean-side condo</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Line</th><th scope="col">A year</th><th scope="col">What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Rent, at a typical listing's $3,470 a month</th><td data-label="A year">About $42,000</td><td data-label="What it is">Money in</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Lodging taxes the guests pay on top</th><td data-label="A year">About $5,000</td><td data-label="What it is">You collect it and send it on</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Property tax at the 6 percent rate</th><td data-label="A year">About $3,980</td><td data-label="What it is">Money out, plus $89.40 in county fees</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Condo dues, which pay for the building's flood policy</th><td data-label="A year">By building</td><td data-label="What it is">We price them for the unit</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cleaning, management, utilities and insurance</th><td data-label="A year">By unit</td><td data-label="What it is">We price them for the unit</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical listing's month is AirROI's figure for every kind of home here, condos and houses together. Compare it with every town on our <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Airbnb income page</a>: <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Compare all nine submarkets</a>. The rules by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="normal-week"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="A normal week">What is a normal week like in Garden City?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Busy in summer and quiet in winter, most of all on the beach road. On Census Day 2020, in April, about 4 in 5 homes along Waccamaw Drive had no one living in them, and about 2 in 3 were held for seasonal or vacation use.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Across all of Garden City, about 4 in 10 homes were vacation homes in 2020, more than twice the share for Horry County. Inland, more owners live here: about half the homes west of Business 17 are taxed as the owner's main home.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes taxed as the owner's main home, by part of Garden City"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes taxed as the owner's main home, by part of Garden City</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ocean side of Waccamaw Drive</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.087" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">Fewer than 1 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Between the marsh and Business 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.371" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 4 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of Business 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.535" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About half</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>South Carolina taxes a home its owner lives in on 4 percent of its value. The rest are taxed at 6 percent: second homes and rentals. Horry County side.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach rules</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County runs the beach from the Surfside Beach town line to the Georgetown County line. Its rules:</p><ul class="c3-gc-rules"><li><strong>Golf carts</strong>On the beach from November 1 to February 28, with a state permit and a licensed driver.</li><li><strong>Dogs</strong>Off the beach from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day. Otherwise on a hand-held leash no longer than 7 feet.</li><li><strong>Shade</strong>Round umbrellas up to 7 feet 6 inches across, and small pop-up cabanas for infants. No tents or canopies, all year.</li><li><strong>Overnight</strong>Nothing may be left on the beach from 7 p.m. to 8 a.m. No alcohol on the beach or the beach accesses.</li></ul><div class="c3-gc-story"><b>An example of a winter day here, not a client's story.</b> A family loads a cooler and buckets into a golf cart. They drive down onto the sand at Garden City. The beach is empty. They build sandcastles, eat lunch and watch the waves for an hour.</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car from the foot of the pier, without traffic. Summer traffic on Business 17 and US 17 adds time.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From the Garden City Pier to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Surfside Beach pier</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The MarshWalk in Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">8 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">8 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Huntington Beach State Park, inside the park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 to 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Market Common</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Coastal Grand Mall</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 25 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Grand Strand Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 30 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Garden City flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of Business 17, no: none of its homes is in a FEMA flood zone. East of Business 17 it is a different place. On the ocean side, 96 in 100 homes are in the high-risk zone, and between the marsh and Business 17, about 54 in 100. In that zone, a lender requires flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood insurance costs much more on the beach strip. Along Waccamaw Drive, the middle federal flood policy on a house cost about $3,260 a year. In the rest of ZIP 29576 it was about $620. A condo building's own flood policy on the strip cost about $17,240 a year at the middle, shared by the owners through their dues.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the big storms did</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In September 1989, Hurricane Hugo's storm surge wiped out up to 90 percent of Garden City's homes. The surge was about 13 feet above sea level. The pier was destroyed, and sand covered roads three blocks inland.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In 2022, Hurricane Ian's surge broke through the dunes in Garden City Beach and flooded parking lots and streets. It left up to three feet of sand on South Waccamaw Drive and removed most of the dunes in Garden City and Surfside Beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">High tides are rising</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">High tides that reach flood level have become more common. At the nearest working tide gauge, they came about 1 or 2 days a year from 1985 to 2004, and about 8 days a year from 2015 to 2024. The sea there has risen about 9 inches since 1957.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Days a year the high tide reached flood level at the nearest tide gauge"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Days a year the high tide reached flood level at the nearest tide gauge</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Years</span><span role="columnheader">Days a year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1985 to 1994</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.142" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 2 days</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1995 to 2004</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.133" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 2 days</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2005 to 2014</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.267" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 3 days</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2015 to 2024</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.7" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 8 days</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">NOAA's outlook for the coming year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8 to 12 days</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>NOAA's minor flood level at Springmaid Pier in Myrtle Beach, the nearest working NOAA tide gauge, about 7 miles north. Decade averages; years missing 60 or more days of readings are left out. The outlook runs May to April.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Army Corps of Engineers' $72 million renourishment, paid for by the federal government, places about 2 million cubic yards of sand along 26 miles of the Grand Strand. Its final phase was working in Surfside Beach and Garden City in July 2026.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer, we pull the flood zone for the exact home and, for a condo, the building's flood policy. Our pages on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">finding out whether a house has flooded</a> and <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance</a> show what we look at.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Garden City each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the middle ocean-side condo, about $320,000, the property tax is about $1,260 a year as your main home, or about $3,980 as a second home or rental. Each bill adds $89.40 in county fees, and the condo dues pay for the building's flood policy.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>A year of owning the middle ocean-side condo, besides the dues</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What you pay</th><th scope="col">As your main home</th><th scope="col">As a second home or rental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Property tax</th><td data-label="As your main home">About $1,260</td><td data-label="As a second home or rental">About $3,980</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">County fees on the bill</th><td data-label="As your main home">$89.40</td><td data-label="As a second home or rental">$89.40</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Your own flood policy on the unit, if you buy one</th><td data-label="As your main home">About $1,560</td><td data-label="As a second home or rental">About $1,560</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes the home you live in on 4 percent of its value, and a second home or rental on 6 percent. A home on the 4 percent rate also skips the 109.1-mill school operating tax. So the same condo pays about 3 times as much tax as a rental as it does as your main home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most Garden City homes, and every ocean-side home, pay 207.3 mills in 2026: the county, the schools, waste management and the Murrells Inlet - Garden City Fire District, which Garden City shares with Murrells Inlet. About 1,300 homes west of Business 17 are in a tax district at 201.0 mills, and about 250 between Waccamaw Drive and Business 17 in one at 234.5. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a> has every rate.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="nearby"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Nearby towns">Garden City, Surfside Beach or Murrells Inlet?</h2><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>Garden City</strong> has no town government, so the county's rules apply, and it has the pier. Most of its beach road is in Georgetown County.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong><a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach</a></strong>, about 6 minutes north by car, pier to pier, is a town with its own government, so its town rules apply.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong><a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet</a></strong> is on the mainland across the marsh. Its MarshWalk is about 8 minutes from the Garden City Pier.</li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="garden-city-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Garden City, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Garden City, SC in Horry County or Georgetown County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Both. The county line crosses the beach about a third of a mile south of the Garden City Pier. The pier is in Horry County, and about 3.2 of the beach road's 5 miles are in Georgetown County.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Garden City part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Garden City has no town government of its own and is not part of any city. Most addresses use Murrells Inlet, ZIP code 29576.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you drive a golf cart on Garden City Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Horry County beach, from November 1 to February 28, with a state permit and a licensed driver.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are dogs allowed on Garden City Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day, on the Horry County beach. At other times, on a hand-held leash no longer than 7 feet.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Garden City, SC safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Garden City has no town police department, because it has no town government.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What schools serve Garden City, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Schools are assigned by address, by the school district of the county the home is in. We look up the assigned schools for any home you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?g=160XX00US4528455" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census 2020</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/monjnvh0/sales-tax-chart-short-term-rentals.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county STR filings</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/351/Hospitality-Accommodations-Tax" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown County</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/garden-city-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA policies</a>, <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ilm/hurricanehugo" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS Hugo</a>, <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ilm/hurricaneian" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS Ian</a>, <a href="https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/stationhome.html?id=8661070" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Springmaid Pier</a>, <a href="https://horrycountysc.gov/about-our-beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county beach rules</a>, <a href="https://www.gardencitypier.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the pier</a>. Our counts from county parcels, flood maps and the past year's deeds, Horry County side. Listings counted in aggregate from CCMLS. Drives from the pier, without traffic.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The ocean side by the pier from above: buildings and beach houses between Waccamaw Drive and the beach, and the salt marsh behind. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">The salt marsh behind the beach strip, with docks from the houses on both edges. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Streets between the marsh and Business 17 from above: houses and yards, a pond, and the salt marsh at the lower right. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Subdivisions west of Business 17 from above: houses on curving streets, ponds, a pool and courts, and woods. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">The Georgetown end near Garden City Point from above: houses on canals with private docks, Waccamaw Drive and the beach. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json