+
+			<p>Doyle Avenue on Pawley&#39;s Island had storm surge flooding in excess of four feet above ground level at this location.&nbsp; This was near the maximum depth of water observed along this portion of the South Carolina coast.</p>
+			</td>
+			<td>
+			<p><a href="/images/ilm/climate/Ian/PawleysSpringAveFloodDamage.jpg"><img alt="Multiple ocean front homes along Springs Avenue (near the 668 address) experienced ground level flooding from surge." src="/images/ilm/climate/Ian/PawleysSpringAveFloodDamage.jpg" style="width: 360px; height: 480px;" /></a></p>
+
+			<p>Multiple ocean front homes along Spring Avenue experienced storm surge flooding. Flowing water piled debris against fixed objects, and sand was scoured and redeposited covering roads and driveways.</p>
