+<p>&nbsp;</p>
+
+<p><span style="font-size:16px;">Strong winds pushed trees across power lines all across Georgetown County. Some roofs were damaged.</span></p>
+
+<p>&nbsp;</p>
+
+<p>&nbsp;</p>
+
+<p><strong><span style="font-size:16px;">Horry County, SC</span></strong></p>
+
+<p><span style="font-size:16px;">In Garden City Beach, storm surge breached the dunes and flooded parking lots and streets. Video shared on social media showed vehicles flooded by several feet of moving water. Debris lines after the storm were noted approximately four feet above ground level in the first floor of some beachfront homes.&nbsp; Upwards of three feet of sand was deposited onto South Waccamaw Drive in Garden City, entombing parked vehicles.</span></p>
+
+<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 725px;">
+	<tbody>
+		<tr>
+			<td>
+			<blockquote class="twitter-tweet">
+			<p dir="ltr" lang="en">Garden City is no stranger to storm surge and we knew they would see coastal flooding. However, with a surge this high the impacts were big! This is from Atalaya Towers from Morgan. <a href="https://twitter.com/jamiearnoldWMBF?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@jamiearnoldWMBF</a> <a href="https://twitter.com/wmbfnews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@wmbfnews</a> <a href="https://twitter.com/hashtag/scwx?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#scwx</a> <a href="https://t.co/3jsyP4nwKi">pic.twitter.com/3jsyP4nwKi</a></p>
+			&mdash; Andrew Dockery (@AndrewWMBF) <a href="https://twitter.com/AndrewWMBF/status/1575946621988241438?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">September 30, 2022</a></blockquote>
+			<script async src="https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script></td>
+			<td>
+			<blockquote class="twitter-tweet">
+			<p dir="ltr" lang="en">Incredible video of storm surge flooding in Inlet Harbor in Garden City yesterday. Never good when ocean waves are breaking on your house. Video via Darius Thompson who was in a rescue vehicle.<a href="https://twitter.com/hashtag/scwx?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#scwx</a> <a href="https://twitter.com/hashtag/ncwx?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#ncwx</a> <a href="https://t.co/vSWaDjhxf6">pic.twitter.com/vSWaDjhxf6</a></p>
+			&mdash; Ed Piotrowski (@EdPiotrowski) <a href="https://twitter.com/EdPiotrowski/status/1576296936436420608?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">October 1, 2022</a></blockquote>
